larmorx-nc holds bit-exact replicas of FSL tools: Rust translations of FSL's source code. They
are derived works of FSL and are distributed under the FSL Licence (see LICENSE): solely for
non-commercial use, without financial return, with the licence's conditions imposed on every
receiver, and with all original and amended source code included. The amended source is the
Rust code of this directory (crates larmorx-nc-*); FSL's original source of the replicated
parts is in fsl-source/ (with MANIFEST.tsv). Both are in every copy of this directory and in
the larmorx-nc wheel. It comes with no warranty (LICENSE). Its source code is published at
https://github.com/karellopez/larmorx (directory crates-nc/). Each translated file names its
licence in an SPDX header and its origin in a comment; each crate's PROVENANCE.md lists the
upstream files it was translated from and the changes made.

The program is a separate work from larmorx (Apache-2.0), which runs it as a separate process
when it is installed. It does not present itself as FSL or as any other upstream tool, and it
is not endorsed by the University of Oxford. For commercial use of FSL, contact Oxford
University Innovation (fsl@innovation.ox.ac.uk, Reference Project 9564, FSL).


